 "brief": "# Merge all build profiles into one\n\nOwner (Brett) request: combine every build profile into ONE new profile on main and delete the others.\n\n## Current profiles (in /opt/axf/_claude/builds/profiles/)\nangel, big-dog, breakroom, current, refactor, urgent — each has orchestrator.json (and possibly pending/plan files).\n\n## Do\n1. Create a new profile `all` (folder _claude/builds/profiles/all/) whose orchestrator.json contains every build from all six profiles, keeping each build's id, status, steps and step states exactly. Merge any other per-profile files (pending JSON, plans, queue, settings) the same way.\n2. On a build id clash between profiles, keep both: suffix the later one with `-<oldprofile>` and note it in STATUS.md.\n3. Keep each build's origin: add a field `fromProfile` with the old profile name.\n4. Make `all` the default/active profile everywhere code, config or UI refers to a profile (profile switcher, planner.plans build target, orchestrator, headless scripts, docs). Any reference to the old names (incl. the `urgent` profile used by planner) must point to `all`. Priority/urgency must stay as a per-build field, not a profile.\n5. Delete the six old profile folders and any registry entries for them.\n6. This supersedes the unfinished `profile-manager` build (5/6): if its branch claude/profile-manager has useful merge code, reuse it; mark profile-manager complete/superseded in the merged file.\n7. Validate: every JSON parses, build count in `all` equals the sum of the old profiles (angel 27, big-dog 3, breakroom 5, current 109, refactor 53, urgent 32 = 229, minus nothing), orchestrator still lists builds correctly, tests/CI pass.\n8. Commit with a clear message. Do not push; it will be landed with build_land.\n\nShipped-product quality. No hard-coded styling. Keep changes minimal outside the profile merge.",
